# TaskFence runs with no environment variables at all.
#
# The policy engine is plain TypeScript, documents are read in your browser
# with pdf.js, and the session record lives in localStorage on the device.
# Deploy it to Vercel with nothing set here and everything works.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# GROQ_API_KEY — optional
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Turns on the AI-assisted document reader (api/understand.ts). It is offered
# only after the built-in deterministic reader has already run, and only for
# the shape of a document: it proposes fields for you to confirm. It never
# fills in an answer, and it has no say whatsoever in what an agent is allowed
# to do — permissions stay in src/lib/policy/engine.ts, which contains no model
# and never calls one.
#
# Without it, the built-in reader is used on its own and the site behaves
# exactly as it otherwise would.
#
# NOTE the name: no VITE_ prefix. Vite inlines VITE_-prefixed variables into
# the JavaScript it ships to every visitor, so a key named VITE_GROQ_API_KEY
# would be public. This one is read server-side only.
#
# Get a key at https://console.groq.com/keys
#
# GROQ_API_KEY=gsk_your_key_here

# Only for your own convenience, never required:
# VITE_PUBLIC_URL=https://your-deployment.vercel.app
